BND-18: clear the averages of periods that fall before REPORT_START

With [REPORT] AVERAGES YES, the REPORT_START gate in postOutputSnapshot()
returned before applyAvgResults(), the only place the averaging
accumulators are reset, so the first saved period averaged every routing
step since START. Reset the accumulators when a period is skipped, as the
patched legacy output_saveResults() does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-18_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..47bdabc 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -6086,6 +6086,9 @@ void SWMMEngine::postOutputSnapshot(double /*dt_step*/) noexcept {
         // periods before ReportStart are not written (no bytes, no Nperiods,
         // no interface row), but the report grid still advances.
         if (report_date < ctx_.options.report_start) {
+            // The averages of an unsaved period must not carry into the
+            // first saved one (legacy output_saveResults, output.c).
+            if (ctx_.options.rpt_averages) avg_.reset();
             hydraulics::TimestepController::reset_output_timer(ctx_);
             return;
         }
